message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "multi-time"
authors:
  - family-names: Friedman
    given-names: Daniel Ari
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6232-9096"
repository-code: "https://github.com/docxology/multi-time"
abstract: "Multi-frequency time series toolkit on sktime — handles patchy and irregular series with frequency detection, gap analysis, ADF/KPSS stationarity and Granger causality tests, then forecasts via Naive, Exponential Smoothing, Theta, AutoARIMA, SARIMAX, and ensembles scored by MAE/MAPE/MASE/RMSSE, with a pytest suite."
license: MIT
